Demonstrates thread-safe atomic frequency incrementing in a Count-Min Sketch row slot using CAS loops

```cpp
void increment(const std::string& key, uint32_t val) {
    for (size_t i = 0; i < depth; ++i) {
        size_t h = hash(i, key) % width;
        uint64_t current = table[i][h].load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
        while (!table[i][h].compare_exchange_weak(current, current + val, std::memory_order_release, std::memory_order_relaxed)) {
            // Retries until successful CAS update
        }
    }
}
